  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Madhya Pradesh District Poverty Initiatives Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s DO is to improve opportunities for the poor and vulnerable, especially women, to meet their own social and economic development objectives in the poorest villages of fourteen districts of the state.  To achieve this objective, the project would: (i) create income security opportunities for the rural poor; (ii)  empower active groups of disadvantaged people; and (iii) promote more effective, accountable and inclusive District and Gram Panchayats (district and village governments) and other local support and service organizations through village organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
